    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] At dev 100b6fbb6e there is no AnalyzerProtocol. Analyzers are @register_analyzer functions typed AnalyzerFunc = Callable[..., AnalysisResult] (registry.py:63), in two call shapes (repo_root[, max_files], by supports_max_files), plus 105 TreeSitterAnalyzer subclasses. The description's analyze()/pass_version/supported_extensions attributes do not exist; the real scope is a callable Protocol replacing Callable[...]. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nDeclare a Protocol class (AnalyzerProtocol) in packages/hypergumbo-core that names every method + attribute a language analyzer must provide: analyze(), pass_version, supported_extensions, etc. Refactor each hypergumbo-lang-* analyzer to structurally fulfill the protocol (no inheritance required). mypy + pyright catch any analyzer that drifts. Closes some INV-jahiv analyzer-parity sub-cases (declared Symbol/Edge fields populated unevenly across languages) at type-check time — protocol requires the methods exist with correct signatures even if the runtime population coverage requires a separate property test."  # 7c85
